ENTRY            E2823   20260816   20260818   20260818       E159
SUBENT        E2823001   20260816   20260818   20260818       E159
BIB                 12         23
TITLE      Investigation toward the production of 236gNp via the
           232Th + 7Li reaction: Synthesis of 236mNp and 234Np
AUTHOR     (A.Nakajima, Y.Hayakawa, A.Nagai, A.Yokoyama, H.Haba,
            Y.Komori, T.Yokokita, Y.Sakakieda, K.Sueki,
            S.Yamasaki, A.Sakaguchi)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNTSU,2JPNKNZ,2JPNIPC)
REFERENCE  (J,ARI,230,112397,2026)
INC-SOURCE Beam intensity is 700 to 1000 particle-nA.
SAMPLE     - Chemical-form of target is element.
           - Physical-form of target is solid. (Th-232 metal
             foils (15 mm x 15 mm x 12.5 um; purity >99 %), and
             electrodeposited Th-232 samples, with an
             electrodeposition surface 12 mm.)
           - Target-thickness is 1.68 to 15.03 mg/cm2.
METHOD     (ACTIV) Irradiated for about 15 h.
           (GSPEC)
FACILITY   (ISOCY,2JPNIPC) AVF cyclotron
DETECTOR   (HPGE) Ge semiconductor detector (Canberra BE2825)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty
           (ERR-1) branching ratio (about 20%)
           (ERR-2,,5.) beam intensity (<5%)
STATUS     (TABLE,,A.Nakajima+,J,ARI,230,112397,2026) Table 1
HISTORY    (20260312C) H.HUANG
ENDBIB              23
COMMON               1          3
ERR-1
PER-CENT
 20.
ENDCOMMON            3
